senses.gloss:
अर्वन् अर्वन्, आ, m. (fr. rt. ऋ), going, run-
ning; epithet of a horse or its driver; a horse;
one of the ten horses of the moon; epithet of Indra;
a short span; (ती), f. a mare; a bawd, a procuress;
(आ, अती, अत्), low, contemptible, inferior, vile.
—अर्व-
नस्, आस्, आस्, अस्, whose nose is like that of a horse.
